* ! < > in a string passed to a macro, and in a dc.b in a vsect (through r68dc): as's MRI
* macros take ! as an escape in <...> and count < and > ("ENTER THE KEY!").
* fixed: db2dd88 2026-10-09 r68togas: ! < > escaped in <...> macro arguments; c32 immediates in parentheses
* expect text: 41ee0000 413c4221 3e00 4e71
* expect data: 454e54455220544845204b45592100 00
 psect string_bang,0,0,0,0,0
MSG macro
 dc.b "\1",0
 endm
 vsect
 dc.b "ENTER THE KEY!",0
 ends
 lea 0(a6),a0
 MSG "A<B!>"
 ends
